The five SOLID principles
Single Responsibility Principle-One class, one responsibility
In Spring Boot:
- Controller handles HTTP requests.
- Service handles business logic.
- Repository handles database operations.
- Notification service handles email/SMS.
--------------------------------------------------------
Open/Closed Principle-Open for extension, closed for modification

Real-world Spring Boot example: Different payment providers, notification channels
-------------------------------------------------------------
Liskov Substitution Principle-Subtypes must be substitutable for their base types
In payment systems, a RefundablePayment should only be implemented by payment methods that genuinely support refunds.
Don't force every payment method to support an operation it cannot perform.


----------------------------------------------------------
Interface Segregation Principle-Small, focused interfaces
BasicPrinter does not support scanning or faxing, but it must implement those methods.


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dependency Inversion Principle-Depend on abstractions, not concrete implementations